{"packet_id":"955acf42be0c78a4","dimensions":{"problem_framing":{"status":"scored","score":2,"event_ids":["A1"],"reason":"A1 separates the objective (is there public evidence to justify a consumer proposition) from the suggested solution. It sets evidence criteria: demand, willingness to pay, or a viable route to market. It lists real alternatives, including expanding B2B, staying put, changing the route to market and targeting other commercial segments. It also names the constraint of Belimo's B2B model and its limited reach to individual buyers. That constraint is stated generically and never developed into an insight a good analyst would worry about missing, so it does not reach 3. The €20,000 / 12-week budget is a self-set assumption, not an observed fact."},"causal_mechanism":{"status":"scored","score":2,"event_ids":["A9","A10"],"reason":"T1 (A9) states who changes behaviour (homeowners), why (durability and energy savings) and how value is captured (own e-commerce or retail at a premium). This covers the chain nominally. However, the capture step ('Belimo gains premium pricing and higher margins by selling directly to consumers') is asserted without engaging the barrier A1 itself flagged: Belimo has no consumer reach and works through OEMs and integrators. The baseline behaviour ('Consumers currently rely on generic thermostats') is asserted without a source. The chain is therefore incomplete, scored 2."},"distinct_theories":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A9","A10"],"reason":"T1 and T2 propose the same product (a premium residential thermostat), the same customer (homeowners) and the same channel (own e-commerce or retail at a premium). They differ only in the purchase motive: savings and durability versus safety and brand trust. They are close rewordings of one idea and imply no different product, customer or channel. Alternatives raised in A1, such as contractor-installed residential components or a B2B extension, never became theories."},"assumptions_predictions":{"status":"scored","score":2,"event_ids":["A9","A10"],"reason":"Assumptions are explicit: willingness to pay a premium, and brand trust transferring from B2B. Predictions are observable: purchase-intent uplift at a stated price premium, and reasons cited in surveys. The thresholds are assumptions, not results. The predictions measure stated intent rather than behaviour. Nearly identical predictions for T1 and T2 would not cleanly put either theory in trouble if they failed. Scored 2, not 3."},"evidence_judgement":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A2","A3","A4","A5","A6","A7","A8","A11"],"reason":"The searches in A2–A8 returned sources, but no assessment of any source was made before the run stopped at A11. Relevant evidence was never weighed. This includes the 2015 residential launch via contractors (belimo-achr-residential-2015), the Airthings consumer revenue decline, and the EIA finding that most households do not program thermostats, which bears on the energy-savings mechanism."},"seeking_challenge":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A2","A3","A4","A5","A6","A7","A8","A11"],"reason":"All searches came before any theory existed (A9, A10) and were near-duplicate exploratory queries. No search was directed against a favoured theory before the stop at A11."},"experiment_design":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A11"],"reason":"No test was proposed or declined before the run stopped at A11. The prediction thresholds in A9 and A10 are not an experiment design."},"revision":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A11"],"reason":"The packet scheduled an update, but it was never delivered (update_delivered=false), and the run stopped at A11. Revision is therefore not_reached."},"recommendation":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A11"],"reason":"A11: 'The investigation stopped before a recommendation (repeated errors).' No recommendation was produced."}},"red_flags":[{"kind":"incomplete","event_ids":["A11"],"reason":"The episode terminated with repeated errors before evidence assessment, testing, revision or a recommendation."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A9","A10"],"reason":"Claims about consumer behaviour are stated as facts without any cited source: 'Consumers currently rely on generic thermostats and low-cost HVAC components' and 'Consumers currently choose HVAC components based on cost and compatibility'. Value capture through direct consumer sales is asserted despite A1 noting Belimo's B2B model and limited consumer reach. Separately, the EIA source (belimo-eia-programmable), which was found in searches but never assessed, reports that most households with programmable thermostats do not program them. That finding sits uneasily with an energy-savings premium-thermostat mechanism."}],"suitable_for_training":false,"screen_reason":"Rejected as incomplete. The run stopped at A11 with no evidence assessment, challenge search, experiment design, revision or recommendation. The reached stages are also weak: the two theories are near-rewordings, and behavioural claims about consumers are stated as unsupported facts. Unreached stages contribute zero to the all-case composite. This is an automated screen, not a judgement of commercial correctness."}
